- **Call sites**: `legacy_auth(<arg>)` → `new_auth(<arg>, scope="read")` or `new_auth(<arg>, scope="write")`
- **Scope assignment**:
  - `scope="write"` (15 files) — files whose return value indicates mutation (`{'created': …}` / `{'updated': …}`) or whose module name contains `_create` / `_update` / `_delete`: `users_create`, `comments_create`, `posts_create`, `uploads_create`, `users_update`, `posts_update`, `users_delete`, `mailer`, `importer`, `notifier`, `billing`, `cleanup`, `sync`, `audit_repo`, `tokens_repo`
  - `scope="read"` (22 files) — all others, which return `{'ok': True}` and have read-oriented names (`_get`, `_list`, `feed`, `search`, etc.)

The `legacy_auth` definition in `app/auth.py` is untouched, as external callers still depend on it.
